ues/105721","id":2829053312,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6on-2A","user":{"login":"AdamLearns","id":60950402,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwOTUwNDAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60950402?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns","html_url":"https://github.com/AdamLearns","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-24T23:16:10Z","updated_at":"2025-04-24T23:16:10Z","body":"Thanks, @Calinou; sounds like I should pass the texture size as a `uniform`, then, based on @clayjohn's response to you in that thread. 👍","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2829053312/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831534665","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105721#issuecomment-2831534665","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105721","id":2831534665,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oxcpJ","user":{"login":"AdamLearns","id":60950402,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwOTUwNDAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60950402?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns","html_url":"https://github.com/AdamLearns","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdamLearns/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-25T22:23:04Z","updated_at":"2025-04-25T22:23:04Z","body":"Small update: I took the hacky/easy route of using the inverse of `TEXTURE_PIXEL_SIZE` so that I didn't need to keep the texture size in-sync between the code and shader sides of things.\n\nIn other words, `vec2 tex_size = vec2(textureSize(TEXTURE, 0));` became `vec2 tex_size = 1.0 / TEXTURE_PIXEL_SIZE;`. The reason I say this is hacky is because floating-point precision should eventually make this number incorrect. E.g. if a texture is, say, 12345 pixels tall, then TEXTURE_PIXEL_SIZE will be `0.00008100445524503848`. You may or may not experience issues depending on how closely the `float` storing that can represent that number.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831534665/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3474359616","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105721#issuecomment-3474359616","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105721","id":3474359616,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7PFoVA","user":{"login":"grampabacon","id":7488087,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0ODgwODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7488087?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grampabacon","html_url":"https://github.com/grampabacon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grampabacon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grampabacon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grampabacon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grampabacon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grampabacon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grampabacon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grampabacon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grampabacon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grampabacon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-31T18:31:01Z","updated_at":"2025-10-31T18:31:01Z","body":"Just ran into this issue and fortunately found this post, managed to get around it by passing in the size as a uniform. I wonder if it would be worth putting a warning in the documentation somewhere like here https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shader_functions.html#texture-functions?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3474359616/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]